CHAPTER II PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of women and children victims of violence is conducted based on the principles of:
a. respect for the rights of victims;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection of victims;
d. best interests of victims;
e. non-discrimination.

Article 3
Protection of women and children victims of violence aims to:
a. prevent all forms of violence against women and children, occurring within the household and/or community;
b. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
c. provide legal assistance;
d. provide services to women and children victims of violence, reporters and witnesses;
e. pursue recovery and social reintegration;
f. increase community participation.

Article 13
(1) Prevention efforts as referred to in Article 12 letter a, include:
a. establishing a prevention and handling network for violence through coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
b. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to violence occurrence;
c. organizing communication, information, and education about violence against women and children;
d. socialization of laws and regulations related to violence against women and children.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the SKPD that has duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE MAYOR OF METRO.
Considering : a. that within every human being are inherent human rights that must be respected, upheld and protected by the state, law, Regional Government and every person for the sake of honor and protection of human dignity and worth;
b. that women and children are among vulnerable groups who tend to become victims of violence and crimes against humanity which constitute violations of human rights, thus requiring protection through regulations that can provide prevention and protection for victims of violence;
c. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of violence;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c above, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children from Violence;
